hose four outermost sides are flat runs of cells.\n\n**What changes.** The output keeps every 8 where it was. The only new cells are colour 4, and they always sit directly against one of a blob's four flat sides. Each group of new cells forms a stepped triangle (a \"roof\") that points outward from that side.\n\n**Measuring the roofs** (pair 1, the upper blob):\n- The top side is row 2, x = 4..8, which is 5 cells long. Above it, row 1 has 4 at x = 5..7 (3 cells) and row 0 has 4 at x = 6 (1 cell).\n- So each layer moving outward loses one cell from each end. In general, layer k covers [a+k, b−k], where a..b is the flat side.\n- The left side is column 3, y = 3..8 (6 cells). It gets column 2, y = 4..7 (4 cells), then column 1, y = 5..6 (2 cells).\n- The lower blob's left side is only 3 cells long (x = 6, y = 15..17). It gets just one cell at (16, 5).\n\n**Roofs that reach the edge are cut off.** In pair 1 the lower blob's bottom roof should have three layers (5, 3, 1 cells), but the grid ends after two. In pair 2 the big blob's left side is column 1, y = 3..10. Its roof is cut after one layer, column 0, y = 4..9. Its top side lies on row 0, so it gets no roof at all. Every other side in pair 2 matches the same layer-by-layer shrinking: the right side gets 6, 4, 2 cells, and the bottom (9 cells) gets 7, 5, 3, 1.\n\n**The rule.** For every 8-object and each of its four extreme sides (top row, bottom row, left column, right column):\n1. Take the extent [a, b] of the object's cells on that extreme line.\n2. Step outward k = 1, 2, …, painting [a+k, b−k] with 4 on background cells only.\n3. Stop when that range becomes empty or the next line is outside the grid.\n\n**On the test input.**\n- The large blob has a top side of row 0, x = 5..9. That roof starts outside the grid, so nothing is drawn.\n- Its bottom side is row 10, x = 5..9. This gives row 11, x = 6..8 and row 12, x = 7.\n- Its left side is column 3, y = 2..8. This gives 5, then 3, then 1 cells in columns 2, 1, 0.\n- Its right side is column 11, y = 2..8. This gives the same 5, 3, 1 pattern in columns 12, 13, 14.\n- The small blob's top side is row 13, x = 14..16. This gives a single cell at (12, 15). Its bottom similarly gives (19, 15).\n- Its left and right sides are 4 cells long. They give 2 cells at x = 12 and at x = 18, each at y = 15..16.\n\nThe program emits one teaching stage per object, after drawing all four roofs of that object.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        cells = o[\"cells\"]\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        # (fixed line index, outward step, axis) ; axis 'row' means side is a row\n        sides = [(y0, -1, 'row'), (y1, 1, 'row'), (x0, -1, 'col'), (x1, 1, 'col')]\n        for line, step, axis in sides:\n            if axis == 'row':\n                xs = [x for y, x in cells if y == line]\n            else:\n                xs = [y for y, x in cells if x == line]\n            a, b = min(xs), max(xs)\n            k = 1\n            while a + k <= b - k:\n                p = line + step * k\n                if axis == 'row':\n                    if p < 0 or p >= H:\n                        break\n                    for x in range(a + k, b - k + 1):\n                        if out[p, x] == bg:\n                            out[p, x] = 4\n                else:\n                    if p < 0 or p >= W:\n                        break\n                    for y in range(a + k, b - k + 1):\n                        if out[y, p] == bg:\n                            out[y, p] = 4\n                k += 1\n        emit(out, f\"Attached shrinking colour-4 triangles to all four flat sides of the 8-object with bbox {o['box']}.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid: every object has a stepped triangle on each side, clipped at the grid edge.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- So each layer moving outward loses one cell from each end."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In general, layer k covers [a+k, b−k], where a..b is the flat side."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Roofs that reach the edge are cut off.** In pair 1 the lower blob's bottom roof should have three layers (5, 3, 1 cells), but the grid ends after two."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"e1962db46dcb949c6110e3212ead5f7df3df0778aa6bc6d56b52b2e12c8d4a1b","task_sha256":"bde182265cebb0f90045dfc60bd4adb8c732096471238d39d56d4e4660fb9700","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
